# Targets chezmoi should delete, not just stop managing.
#
# Dropping a file from the source tree only makes chezmoi forget it — the copy
# already applied to a machine stays on disk. For a Neovim plugin spec that is
# not "unmanaged", it is "still loaded by lazy.nvim", so the old colorscheme
# would keep installing itself alongside token forever.
#
# Paths are target paths relative to $HOME, same as .chezmoiignore.

# Replaced by token (dot_config/nvim/lua/plugins/token.lua). The palettes for
# kanagawa are still in terminal-tools and still reachable via `theme pick`;
# this only removes the editor half.
.config/nvim/lua/plugins/kanagawa-paper.lua
